    <!-- Legal -->
    <string name="legal_privacy_heading">PianoFlow Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="legal_privacy_body">Last updated: September 2026\n\nYour privacy is important to us. PianoFlow does not collect, sell, or transmit any personal data or recorded melodies to external servers without your permission.\n\n1. Local Storage: All song scores, lesson progress, and recorded piano files are stored securely on your local device.\n\n2. Audio &amp; Recordings: Audio recordings are processed on-device and only exported or shared when you explicitly initiate sharing.\n\n3. Subscriptions &amp; Billing: In-app purchases are securely processed through official store billing. We do not store your credit card or payment credentials.\n\n4. Contact: For privacy questions, contact support@pianoflow.app.</string>
    <string name="legal_terms_heading">PianoFlow Terms of Service</string>
    <string name="legal_terms_body">Last updated: September 2026\n\nBy downloading or using PianoFlow, you agree to the following terms:\n\n1. License: PianoFlow grants you a revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable personal license to learn and play piano for personal entertainment and educational use.\n\n2. Songs &amp; Intellectual Property: All musical arrangements included within the application are in the public domain or independently created. You own full rights to original songs you compose and record using PianoFlow.\n\n3. Subscriptions: PianoFlow Premium provides recurring weekly, monthly, and yearly options. Subscriptions automatically renew unless cancelled at least 24 hours prior to the end of the billing period via your account settings.\n\n4. Disclaimer: The software is provided \'as is\' without warranties of any kind.</string>

